// src/vm.h's FRAMES_MAX (256) bounds nested Lox calls with a controlled
// runtime error, not a real machine stack fault: src/vm.cpp's own
// interpret() pushes the top-level script as CallFrame 0 before the body
// runs, so 254 nested calls from within the script is the deepest that
// stays under the ceiling, and 255 overflows it (verified against
// build-release/loxpp). A backend whose calling convention recurses its
// own host call stack has no such ceiling on its own, and must build one
// to match, or this depth silently succeeds where native fails.
fun down(n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    return down(n - 1);
}
print down(255);
